  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They led after the first inning. Everything after that was about losing ground.",
    "what_this_means": "Ten runners left on base. Not one of them scored. The offense found chances in the fifth. Runners on second and third with one out. And came away empty. They did it again in the seventh with three more left behind. Trevor McDonald gave them five and a third innings of three-run ball, which should have been enough. The bullpen held perfectly: three relievers, three scoreless innings, three strikeouts. But the game required runs, not just innings. They never made it matter.",
    "what_to_watch": "This is inconsistency wearing a new mask. The pitching was good. The opportunity was there. The execution was not. They're now 33-48, 18.5 back, and they don't have room to squander nights like this. Games where the starter does his job and the relief does its job and the only thing missing is production when it counts. That absence is becoming the story.",
